  "notes": "USAGE:\nVery common in everyday conversation about relationships. This is the passive form of {振|ふ}る (to dump someone), but it is used so frequently that it functions almost as its own word.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {彼氏|かれし}に{振|ふ}られる (to be dumped by one's boyfriend)\n- {彼女|かのじょ}に{振|ふ}られる (to be dumped by one's girlfriend)\n- {告白|こくはく}して{振|ふ}られる (to confess and be rejected)\n- {振|ふ}られた{経験|けいけん} (experience of being rejected)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {断|ことわ}られる: to be refused — broader term, not specific to romance\n- フラれる: alternate spelling using katakana フラ, common in casual writing",
